# One for both images, which build from the root (`_standards/tooling.md` §8.2), with the list
# from the pnpm page (_doc-lib/pnpm.md#docker). Every pattern carries `**/`: without it Docker only
# matches at the root of the context, and `backend/.env` and `backend/node_modules` go into the
# image (finding in aporta, SEGURANCA.md).

# The machine's dependency tree (wrong architecture) and previous build output: the image
# installs and compiles everything from the code (DECISIONS.md #290).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.output
**/coverage
**/tmp

# History and documentation do not go into the image.
.git
**/.gitignore
.github
**/*.md

# A secret never enters the build context. The frontend's `.env.production` is the exception: it
# only carries public `VITE_*` variables, which the build embeds in the bundle (`backend.md` §6).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!frontend/.env.production

**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
